hi I'm Annie whoo and I'm a mathematics  teacher a challenge with the subject of  mathematics specifically is that one of  the most amazing things about  mathematics I think is that it is  timeless you know once you prove  something is true in mathematics it's  true forever and I love that we can  study ancient theorems and we don't have  to update them or revise them because  people have discovered new evidence they  are eternal and still true whether we  discovered them centuries ago or last  year and I think that's brilliant but at  the same time it presents a challenge  for us attention because while the  subject is timeless the way the subject  is applied in the real world is not and  there's a real temptation to you know  hold to these ways of the past because  mathematics is still true it's  arithmetic is still true calculus is  still true but to not move with the  future and to say you know what as a  profession and as a discipline we still  have to stay up-to-date we want to  maintain that tension between  prizing these things that are eternally  true but also making sure we connect to  students in the real world the world  they live in now and the ways that  mathematics applies in ways that didn't  happen in decades and centuries past  I think holding that tension is  difficult to do but it's really  important if we want our students to  understand this timeless beauty of the  subject but also see it in connection to  their actual lives  [Music]
 

